# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BrandFactory — Next frontend.
#
# Two backends, and the split is by feature, not by call.
#
#   * The BrandFactory API (Hono, `packages/server`) serves identity, workspaces
#     and brands. It is reached through `src/lib/api/bf-client.ts`.
#   * The Operations Hub fixtures serve the other fifteen areas, which arrived
#     with this shell and have no BrandFactory backend. They are reached through
#     `src/lib/api/client.ts` and answered from `src/fixtures/`.
#
# The NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars below are inlined into the JS bundle. Never put a secret
# in one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── The BrandFactory API ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where `next.config.ts` proxies `/api/*`. The Hono server's dev port.
#
# Server-side only — the rewrite is resolved by the Next server and this value
# never reaches the browser, which is why it carries no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:3001

# Only for a split-origin deploy (this app on one host, the API on another).
# Leave unset and the client calls `/api`, which the proxy above forwards — one
# origin, and no CORS configuration to keep in step. Set it, and the server's
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS must list this app's origin.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BF_API_URL=https://api.example.com

# ── Sign-in ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `local`    — paste the dev token `pnpm -F @brandfactory/db db:seed` prints.
#              Matches the server's own default (AUTH_PROVIDER=local).
# `supabase` — magic link and Google, against the project below.
#
# This must agree with the server's AUTH_PROVIDER, or the page offers a door the
# API will not open.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_PROVIDER=local

# Required when NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_PROVIDER=supabase. The anon key is public by
# design — it is the browser-side key, and row-level security is what protects
# the data behind it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# ── The Operations Hub fixtures ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to `mock`, which answers every request from `src/fixtures/` via
# `src/lib/api/mock.ts` — no backend needed, and nothing is stored. `live` sends
# real requests to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL instead, which currently nothing serves.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MODE=mock

# Only read when NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MODE=live.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Only needed against a backend that gates on a shared token.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_TOKEN=
